__pycache__/
*.pyc
docs/transcripts/
.claude/worktrees/
# Experiment run output (records.jsonl / summary.json / report.md). A run that
# is worth keeping gets its report copied into docs/plans/ deliberately.
prototype/runs/
# Terraform working directories and any state that ends up on disk. The
# provider lock files (.terraform.lock.hcl) are deliberately NOT ignored.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
crash.log

# Rust build output and the stores. Both are reproducible — `.loom-store` from
# the pinned corpus by `task store:seed`, `.loom-store-generated` from that plus
# a run's records by `task store:harvest` — so they are derived data, not
# fixtures. They are kept apart deliberately: `.loom-store` is the curated seed
# the equivalence tests read, and harvesting into it would make
# `test_the_seeded_store_carries_the_oracle_sidecars_unchanged` false by adding
# objects the oracle's corpus document does not contain.
#
# The diversity harvest adds two more of the same kind — `.loom-store-diverse`
# and `.loom-store-sizematch`, both rebuilt from the recorded runs by
# `task store:diverse` / `task store:sizematch`. A glob rather than three more
# literal lines, so the next arm's store is ignored without anyone remembering
# to add it; `.loom-store` itself is still listed explicitly because the glob
# would not match it.
store/target/
.loom-store/
.loom-store-*/

# The L0 differential export (docs/plans/2026-08-14-production-language-decision.md,
# Track P). Derived data: `task differential:export` reproduces it byte for byte
# from the tree, so the generator is the artifact and the JSONL is its output.
prototype/differential/*.jsonl

prototype/experiment/phase_a.local.json
prototype/experiment/phase_a.smoke.json
prototype/experiment/phase_a.remote.json
